  "title": "Values and typeof",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Kinds you can print\n\nEvery value has a kind. `typeof 3` is `\"number\"`. `typeof \"3\"` is `\"string\"`. `typeof null` is `\"object\"` — that answer is a leftover bug. Do not treat `null` as a bag of fields.\n\nExport `kindOf` so a hidden test can call it. Print the kind of the number 3."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "typeof-null",
      "promptMd": "`typeof null` prints which string?",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "null",
          "md": "`null`"
        },
        {
          "id": "object",
          "md": "`object`",
          "misconceptionId": "null-is-object-ok"
        },
        {
          "id": "undefined",
          "md": "`undefined`"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "object"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "typeof-number",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> Return and print `typeof 3` (`number`).",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "files/main.js",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/hidden.test.js",
          "role": "hidden-test"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "stdout",
          "equals": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "ast",
          "query": "typeof"
        },
        {
          "type": "js-assert"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "`typeof` is an operator, not a function you must call with extra punctuation."
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "Export `kindOf` so the hidden test can call `kindOf(3)`."
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "function kindOf(v) { return typeof v }\nconsole.log(kindOf(3))\nmodule.exports = { kindOf }"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": "Every value has a kind: number, text, or true and false. You need this before any list."
